                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 6 at 2:47PM HST until September 6 at 5:30PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "FFWHFO\n\nThe National Weather Service in Honolulu has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe island of Oahu in Honolulu County\n\n* Until 530 PM HST.\n\n* At 247 PM HST, Doppler radar indicated moderate to locally heavy\nshowers over windward Oahu, with the heaviest rain falling at a\nrate of 1 to 3 inches per hour over the central Koolau Mountains.\nRapid rises in water levels in the Waiahole and Waikane Streams\nindicate that flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Gauges reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nHonolulu, Kahaluu, Waiahole, Ahuimanu, Waikane, Kaneohe, Kaaawa,\nAiea, Kaneohe Marine Base, Halawa, Moanalua and Pearl City.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
