                "senderName": "NWS Grand Forks ND",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 6 at 6:37PM CDT until September 7 at 12:30AM CDT by NWS Grand Forks ND",
                "description": "FFWFGF\n\nThe National Weather Service in Grand Forks has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSouthwestern Otter Tail County in west central Minnesota...\n\n* Until 1230 AM CDT.\n\n* At 637 PM CDT, the public reported thunderstorms producing heavy\nrain in Multiple reports of reports of stalled vehicles and flooded\nroads. Between 3 and 4 inches of rain have fallen. Additional\nrainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches are possible in the warned area.\nFlash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Public reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nFergus Falls, southwestern Ottertail Lake, Battle Lake,\nsouthwestern Star Lake, Underwood, Elizabeth, southeastern\nMaplewood State Park, Carlisle, Amor, Phelps, Edwards, Maplewood,\nGlendalough and Fergus Falls Airport.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nPlease report observed flooding to local emergency services or law\nenforcement and request they pass this information to the National\nWeather Service when you can do so safely.",
                "response": "Avoid",
